# The staging tree comes from `git archive`, so this file is a second fence,
# not the first one. The uv server type specifically forbids shipping a
# resolved environment: a bundle must carry pyproject.toml and let the host
# resolve, never server/lib or server/venv.
.venv/
server/lib/
server/venv/
uv.lock
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
config.json
.DS_Store

# Developer tooling that `git archive` cannot leave out because it is tracked
# and lives under `src/`. `src/td_atlas/component/ruff.toml` declares the
# globals TouchDesigner injects, so the linter does not read `op` and `me` as
# undefined names; it configures a check that is never run from a bundle. The
# staging tree is meant to be source, metadata, licence and readme — nothing
# else — and a lint config is none of the four.
src/td_atlas/component/ruff.toml
